! The unaveraged selection lives in the lattice, where element parameters belong.
! The default 2-period ramps carry two priced end effects (manual sec:unaveraged):
! their slippage deficit is compensated exactly by the mode's built-in phase jump,
! and their reduced coupling length costs ~2% in ln power per segment -- real field
! physics of adiabatic ends, deliberately not hidden.

call, file = aramis.bmad
fel_unaveraged = 1
wiggler::*[FEL_TRACKING] = fel_unaveraged
